This project is a Real-Time Face Attendance System built with Python 3.10, OpenCV, and the deep learning library DeepFace. It utilizes the high-accuracy VGG-Face model to identify individuals from a live webcam feed. The system works in two stages: first, encode_faces.py trains the database by processing student images (found in data/students/) and creating embeddings (in representations_vgg_face.pkl); second, mark_attendance.py runs the live camera, identifies the user, and automatically logs the entry time into a persistent attendance.csv file (found in data/attendance/). To set up, users must first install dependencies via requirements.txt and ensure their webcam is accessible.